  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A point charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#181;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is placed at the origin. At what location on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis should a point charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#181;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> be placed so that the net electric field is zero at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
